---
name: review-rounds
description: A reviewer approves, rejects or asks for a revision; each revision goes back for another round.
engine: 0.2.0-lab.1
roles: [lead, reviewer]
---
"""
Review one change in at most three rounds. Approved is the reviewer's
assertion that the change is ready; it grants nothing beyond the reviewer's
role.
"""
contract @1h => expired

"""
Send the change and the question. When the reviewer asks for a revision,
change the work and resend the request saying what changed, or withdraw.
"""
role lead

"""
Review only the latest request. Decide approve, revise or reject, with
evidence. Ask for a revision only with specific, actionable changes.
"""
role reviewer

"""
The change to review, the question and, in a later round, what changed.
"""
type request
  text: text(1..2000)

"""
The reviewer's decision on the request it names, with findings and evidence.
"""
type review
  source: ref(request)
  decision: enum(approve|revise|reject)
  text: text(1..4000)

"""
The lead stops the review. Say why in the conversation around it.
"""
type withdraw

"""
The lead opens the first round.
"""
state new
  """
  Send the request. The reviewer owes one decision on it.
  """
  lead -> reviewer: request() as req awaits reviewing
    """
    The change is ready as sent.
    """
    => review(source=$req, decision=approve) & approved
     """
     The change needs specific revisions before it can be approved.
     """
     | review(source=$req, decision=revise) & revising
     """
     The change should not proceed in any revised form.
     """
     | review(source=$req, decision=reject) & rejected
     """
     No decision arrived within ten minutes of the request.
     """
     | @10m & stalled

"""
The reviewer reviews the latest request. A decision on an earlier request no
longer counts. A fourth round ends the run as exhausted.
"""
state reviewing max_entries 3 => exhausted
  """
  Stop the review before the reviewer decides.
  """
  lead -> reviewer: withdraw() => withdrawn

"""
The reviewer asked for a revision. Revise and resend, or withdraw.
"""
state revising
  """
  Resend the revised change and say what changed since the last round.
  """
  lead -> reviewer: request() as req => reviewing
  """
  Stop instead of revising.
  """
  lead -> reviewer: withdraw() => withdrawn

"""
The reviewer approved the latest request. Acting on it is a separate decision.
"""
end approved

"""
The reviewer rejected the change. Do not resend it in this run.
"""
end rejected

"""
The lead withdrew the review. Send nothing more.
"""
end withdrawn

"""
No decision arrived in time; the lead must decide how to recover.
"""
end stalled

"""
Three rounds were used without approval or rejection. Keep the last review
for recovery.
"""
end exhausted
